  "stem": "A pendulum made of a uniform wire of cross-sectional area A has time period T. When an additional mass M is added to its bob, the time period changes to TM. If the Young's modulus of the material of the wire is Y then 1/Y is equal to: (g = gravitational acceleration)",
  "options": {
    "A": "$\\left\\lbrack 1 - {(\\frac{T_{M}}{T})}^{2} \\right\\rbrack\\frac{A}{Mg}$",
    "B": "$\\left\\lbrack 1 - {(\\frac{T}{T_{M}})}^{2} \\right\\rbrack\\frac{A}{Mg}$",
    "C": "$\\left\\lbrack {(\\frac{T_{M}}{T})}^{2} - 1 \\right\\rbrack\\frac{A}{Mg}$",
    "D": "$\\left\\lbrack {(\\frac{T_{M}}{T})}^{2} - 1 \\right\\rbrack\\frac{Mg}{A}$"
  },
  "answer": {
    "keys": [
      "C"
    ]
  },
